// Host approvals document for the lab exec node. Applied LOCALLY on the lab VM before pairing
// (local exec approvals default to security "full" / ask "off" until set), and re-applied from
// the Pi with:  openclaw approvals set --node lab-exec --file approvals-lab-exec.json5
// Allowlisted binaries run silently for the lab agent; anything else asks; no answer = deny.
// strictInlineEval (in openclaw.json) still forces approval for python -c, node -e, sed, awk, find -exec.
//
// FULL PATHS, and the agent must call them by full path (see config/lab-AGENTS.md).
// Verified in OpenClaw 2026.10.9 source (analyzeNodeApprovalRequirement / matchAllowlist): before
// dispatching to a node, the Gateway re-checks this allowlist ON THE PI, resolving the executable
// with an empty PATH. A bare name ("ls") never resolves there, so bare patterns never match and
// every command prompts. A full path resolves only if that file also exists on the Pi, and then
// matches a full-path pattern (bare patterns deliberately skip commands given with a path).
// So every binary listed here must exist at the same path on BOTH the lab VM and the Pi.
// Checked 2026-11-01: git, docker, ls, cat are /usr/bin on both. make and rg are /usr/bin on the
// Pi; install them on the VM (apt install make ripgrep) for these entries to be useful.
// npm/pnpm are on neither machine's PATH, so they are left out (they would always prompt).
{
  version: 1,
  defaults: { security: "allowlist", ask: "on-miss", askFallback: "deny", autoAllowSkills: false },
  agents: {
    lab: {
      allowlist: [
        { pattern: "/usr/bin/git" }, { pattern: "/usr/bin/docker" }, { pattern: "/usr/bin/ls" },
        { pattern: "/usr/bin/cat" }, { pattern: "/usr/bin/make" }, { pattern: "/usr/bin/rg" },
      ],
    },
  },
}
